# Parameters of the mutation score push (docs/mutation-push.md): the 2,420 mutants of the
# 73536f0 campaign re-run under the committed suite and classified formally.
# Source campaign.env first (its CAMP holds the design/ and results/equiv/ that the push
# reuses), then this file, then run the commands in README.md, section "Mutation score push".
#
# the push's own work directory, as run (results/head-design, results/kill-design_final,
# results/kill-design_k6, results/kill-design_k7, results/formal1, results/einv-invonly)
PUSH_DIR=${PE_WORK:?set PE_WORK to the cluster work directory}/mutation97
# a fresh directory for a re-run with the repository scripts
PUSH=${PE_WORK:?set PE_WORK to the cluster work directory}/mutation-push
# test trees: the whole-suite stage ran on c118027 (66 tests; run_mutant.py stage `suite`,
# called `head` in the push); the kill stages on c118027 plus the test_kill_*.py modules
# committed in aa07868 (byte-identical to those of the last kill stage, k7)
HEAD_COMMIT=c118027
KILL_COMMIT=aa07868
KILL_MODULES="test_kill_decode test_kill_blocked test_kill_pc test_kill_mover test_kill_regs test_kill_xfer test_kill_host test_kill_events test_kill_pins test_kill_edges test_kill_fifo"
# formal_mutant.py options of job 23977941 (miter + ABC)
FORMAL_ARGS="--props strict --pdr-seconds 60 --abc-timeout 150"
# controls of job 23977941: six killed by test_smoke, six of the 116 proven equivalent
FORMAL_CONTROLS="1099 1185 1164 1021 1249 1010 1332 1849 102 46 2229 1726"
# negative controls of equiv_inv.py (job 23986701): three killed mutants
EINV_CONTROLS="43 1010 1099"
